This program exists to prove that a raw OS thread's mutator slot is released when
the thread exits (#1801). A leaked slot stays `running` forever, so every later
rendezvous expires — which is silent: nothing corrupts, no output changes,
collection simply stops. That makes the count of ABANDONED collections the only
oracle, and this program is built so the defect is its only possible cause: the
child contains no loop and so attempts no collection of its own, and the parent's
measuring loop runs after `threadRelease`, by which point it is the only live
mutator. See ../thread/exitprops.
